
# <short imperative summary, max 50-72 chars> (e.g., Fix RMD divisor rounding)
# Leave a blank line between the subject line above and section (A) below.
# Lines starting with '#' are stripped automatically by Git when you commit.

(A) Classification: 
# Select one: Bug | Feature | Performance | Cosmetic
# - Bug:         Fixes unexpected behavior, wrong math, or a crash
# - Feature:     Adds new capability, UI workflow, parser, or configuration
# - Performance: Improves runtime, memory usage, caching, or bundle size
# - Cosmetic:    Formatting, wording, layout polish, comments, or docs-only edits

(B) Severity: 
# Select one: Low | Medium | High
# - High:   Security/privacy regression, data loss, crash, or wrong core math/tax
# - Medium: Partial feature breakage, degraded UX, or notable performance impact
# - Low:    Minor polish, documentation update, or non-blocking improvement

(C) Description:
# Summarize what changed and why. Reference affected modules, design choices,
# edge cases, and related issue or PR numbers.

(D) Privacy and Security Implications:
# Note any impact on Privacy Shield (Modes A/B/C), Demo Mode scaling/aliasing,
# localhost/session auth, 0600 file permissions, PII/leak gates, or LLM/MCP tools.
# Write "None" if there is no privacy or security impact, and briefly state why.

(E) Testing notes:
# List commands run and observed results against isolated fixture portfolios
# (e.g., `make test`, `make test-security`, `make test-full`, `make fixtures-check`,
# or manual browser/UI verification steps).
